WEBVTT

00:00:01.070 --> 00:00:03.260
My passionate Idol Activities,

00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:06.360
Aikatsu! is about to start!

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:11.900
Though it's still the chilly month of March, Ran is burning hot!

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:16.980
That's because Ran's favorite brand,

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:22.410
Spicy Ageha, is holding a seasonal audition to determine their representative model.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.360
Ran's sure pumped up.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:27.970
She's a woman on fire.

00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:30.740
Love you! So awesome!

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:32.270
She really is.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:38.260
Being praised by Yurika-sama is a once-in-a-lifetime event.

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:40.440
She'd better be grateful.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:42.050
Right, more like that.

00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:43.980
<i>That's</i> our Yurika-tan.

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:47.180
Normal-mode Yurika-chan's plenty cute too though.

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:50.120
Come now, calling me cute...

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:52.690
If you're not careful I'll suck your blood!

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:54.740
Thanks for waiting around for me.

00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:58.450
Don't worry, it's fun to watch you practice your walking.

00:00:58.450 --> 00:00:59.900
It's educational.

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:02.710
It makes me feel like I have to try hard too.

00:01:02.710 --> 00:01:07.580
Yurika-sama isn't even hiding the fact
 that she isn't not cheering you on.

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:09.340
So which is it?

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:11.860
I-I <i>said</i> I'm cheering for you!

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:13.360
I'm rooting for you too.

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:14.250
Me too.

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:15.840
Otome too!

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:20.470
Thank you. I plan to leave everything on the stage.

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:25.940
May Ran be chosen to be Spicy Ageha's 
representative model.

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:27.980
I have no doubt you'll pass.

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:29.110
Thanks.

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:48.350
Hi, signalize!

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:53.730
The answer lies on the other side of the sky

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:53.710
kotae wa motto takai sora no kanata

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:55.600
No, that's wrong

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:55.600
iie chigau yo

00:01:55.920 --> 00:02:00.980
I can see with my eyes that it's at the end of the Earth

00:01:55.920 --> 00:02:00.980
boku no me ni mo mieta chi no hate

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:02.770
Do that signalize!

00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:07.950
Something's starting to bubble up

00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:07.950
hageshiku natta mune no atsui powaa

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:11.910
From the burning power in my raging heart

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:11.910
sou da minagiru nanika ga

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:15.450
So I'll believe in the present

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:15.450
dakara ima wo shinjite

00:02:15.790 --> 00:02:20.620
And start today since it's more than a faint desire

00:02:15.790 --> 00:02:20.620
hajimeyou tada no akogare ja nai

00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:21.960
Chance for me

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:27.260
Dreams can make even the harshest nightmare pleasant

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:27.260
zankoku na yume ga yume de yume ni narunda

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:31.470
It's just another challenge on the way

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:31.470
hora chousen matteru yo

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:36.390
Where are we headed?

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:36.390
kimi to mukau basho wa doko darou

00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:40.140
Into a brilliant hope

00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:40.140
mabushii kibou no naka e

00:02:40.730 --> 00:02:47.400
Where do we want to go? Let's go find it right now

00:02:40.730 --> 00:02:47.400
nozomu basho wa doko darou sagashi ni ikou yo shuppatsu da

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:50.780
Where we're headed

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:50.780
mukau basho wa mirai no

00:02:51.570 --> 00:02:54.660
is into our hopes for the future

00:02:51.570 --> 00:02:54.660
bokura no kibou no naka ni

00:02:54.990 --> 00:03:02.000
Our destination is the future, the light is our signal Let's go, go!

00:02:54.990 --> 00:03:02.000
nozomu basho wa mirai no kagayaki ga aizu let's go, go

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.460
Good morning, honeys!

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:15.820
I'm sure you've all realized, but spring's coming soon!

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:18.200
Um...

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:19.860
You mean it's almost springtime?

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:22.190
Yes! Exactly right, Kiriya.

00:03:22.190 --> 00:03:25.850
And there's one more thing that's getting closer. What?

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:26.900
What is it?

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:27.900
I wonder...

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:29.810
Does he mean the Spicy Ageha audition?

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:35.310
It's a graduation ceremony!
Prepare yourselves!

00:03:36.050 --> 00:03:37.310
It's graduation!

00:03:37.310 --> 00:03:38.320
Oh yeah...

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:41.320
It <i>is</i> March after all. The third-years are graduating.

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:46.190
Here's a video message from Beauti-Full Moon of the planning committee.

00:03:46.190 --> 00:03:46.830
Go!

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:48.580
Beauti-Full what?

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:50.620
I think he means Mizuki-chan.

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:53.250
Good afternoon, everyone.

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:57.590
As the graduation ceremony is drawing nearer, I have a very important announcement.

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:01.820
Here at Starlight Academy, this year's graduation event

00:04:01.820 --> 00:04:05.040
will include a fashion show held by the current students.

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:06.440
There'll be a fashion show!

00:04:06.440 --> 00:04:07.640
It sounds exciting!

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:15.000
Students from the high school division along with alumnae of the academy will be attending.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:19.880
Let's all work together to show our seniors what a wonderful show we can put on!

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:24.840
I'm personally inviting you—wouldn't you like to try standing on that stage?

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:27.120
Those who wish to apply, please contact me!

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:33.000
You really didn't waste any time, Ichigo.

00:04:34.770 --> 00:04:36.230
Mizuki-san!

00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:39.250
Are you applying, Hoshimiya?

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:41.510
Yes, for Ran!

00:04:43.010 --> 00:04:48.100
Pardon, was <i>this</i> the mouth that said
 that without even consulting me?

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:49.510
Sorry, I couldn't help it.

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:52.290
I totally understand Ichigo-tan's feelings!

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:55.940
Me too. And Ran, you have a lot of 
fans in the graduating class,

00:04:55.940 --> 00:04:58.900
so I'm sure they'll be happy you're in it!

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:04.570
That's right, it's not like Yurika-sama doesn't not think the same way after all.

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:06.410
Like I said, pick one clearly.

00:05:06.980 --> 00:05:09.910
I'm saying that Yurika-sama agrees with her.

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:12.680
Anyway, let's show them a wonderful show!

00:05:12.680 --> 00:05:15.670
I wonder why that sounds like a bad pun when Ichigo says it?

00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:18.800
It sounds perfectly normal when Mizuki-san says it.

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:20.170
It's not a joke!

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:22.160
I guess it's a difference in your personalities.

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:23.170
Yeah.

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:30.930
Moving on, all of us underclassmen quickly got to work 
preparing the sending-off event for the graduating seniors. {unfortunately the word graduate works differently from 卒業生 -- you're not one until after you've graduated}

00:05:31.390 --> 00:05:35.820
For the fashion show's sign, want to try something different and make a really flashy one?

00:05:35.820 --> 00:05:37.310
Sounds good!

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:41.070
Uh, Ichigo, half of your face is pretty flashy itself.

00:05:44.840 --> 00:05:46.470
It's pretty late.

00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:48.990
But even though the sun hasn't set...

00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:50.830
It's cold!

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:53.520
Oh, Ran.

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:54.950
You're drenched in sweat.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:58.450
Probably because I ran twice the usual today.

00:05:58.450 --> 00:05:59.330
Twice?!

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:02.710
I want to prepare my body as much as I can for the audition.

00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:04.720
You're really giving it your all.

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:05.720
Yeah.

00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:08.960
There's someone I absolutely have to overtake.

00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:11.470
Someone to overtake?

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:15.470
Oh yeah, I forgot that I never told you two about her.

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:19.980
I'm sure you've seen her before— she's a third-year here. {bullshit}

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:22.380
I know her, she's Shinjou Ema-san.

00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:24.920
Not only does she work as a model,

00:06:24.920 --> 00:06:29.030
she's also famous as an expert stylist using Aikatsu cards.

00:06:29.030 --> 00:06:29.690
Right.

00:06:29.690 --> 00:06:31.490
So she's into fashion.

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:36.250
Yeah, and no matter what Ema-san wears, she can always make her clothes sparkle.

00:06:36.710 --> 00:06:39.750
She's the person Ran wants to overtake.

00:06:40.640 --> 00:06:42.600
Unless I can overtake her,

00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:45.820
I won't be able to become the 
representative model of Spicy Ageha.

00:06:45.820 --> 00:06:48.290
So she'll be entering the audition too.

00:06:48.290 --> 00:06:49.260
She will.

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:54.010
The first time I met her, she was holding 
an amazing amount of cards...

00:06:58.910 --> 00:07:01.420
So I see you like Spicy Ageha.

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:02.530
How...

00:07:02.530 --> 00:07:04.320
It's written on your face.

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:08.400
Clothes are wonderful.

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:11.700
They can make you so happy just from looking at them.

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:12.910
Yes.

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:15.820
I truly love them.

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:21.910
Unlike me, Ema-san

00:07:21.910 --> 00:07:26.470
likes not just Spicy Ageha, but all different sorts of clothes.

00:07:26.470 --> 00:07:29.900
But Spicy Ageha means everything to me...

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:32.960
That's why I definitely don't want to lose.

00:07:32.960 --> 00:07:33.940
Right.

00:07:33.940 --> 00:07:37.100
We'll do everything we can to help you!

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:47.690
Hey, Ran. When exactly was it that
 you fell in love with Spicy Ageha?

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:50.960
Probably around my third year of elementary school.

00:07:50.960 --> 00:07:56.100
My hair was short back then, so 
people often mistook me for a guy.

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:58.050
What? For a boy?!

00:07:58.050 --> 00:07:58.770
<i>You?!</i>

00:07:58.770 --> 00:07:59.700
Yeah.

00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:04.460
It was quite a while back, but I've also
 done modeling for boy's clothing.

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:08.650
My god! Pictures of Ran as a boy must be ultra rare!

00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:11.040
I never knew!

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:13.970
How can Kiriya Aoi be called an idol fan like this?!

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:15.790
I'm in despair.

00:08:15.790 --> 00:08:17.220
Hey, do you think I could see those—

00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:20.700
So how did you decide to change 
your image to your current one?

00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:21.820
I didn't do anything.

00:08:21.820 --> 00:08:23.990
Huh? You didn't do anything?

00:08:23.990 --> 00:08:28.430
Yeah. It's just... the first time I wore Spicy Ageha,

00:08:28.430 --> 00:08:32.610
my heart started pounding, and it
 was like I became a different person.

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:34.990
I thought, "I love these clothes!"

00:08:34.990 --> 00:08:39.190
I thought that I wanted to change to become a person who befit those clothes...

00:08:39.740 --> 00:08:43.000
Those feelings you had were what shaped how you are today.

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:46.840
I'm not sure about that, but I do know that I love Spicy Ageha.

00:08:46.840 --> 00:08:50.130
I know that at least these feelings won't lose out to Ema-san.

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:50.980
Yeah.

00:08:50.980 --> 00:08:52.320
Let's win this.

00:08:52.320 --> 00:08:54.760
Then let's do three hundred more crunches.

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:56.760
You trying to kill me?

00:08:57.260 --> 00:09:01.790
And so, the day of the audition for becoming Spicy Ageha's representative model arrived.

00:09:05.240 --> 00:09:06.970
I wonder how it went?

00:09:06.970 --> 00:09:09.670
I'm pretty sure it's about the time the results are announced.

00:09:09.670 --> 00:09:12.780
Ah, geez! Time for crunches!

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:14.390
Why crunches...

00:09:14.390 --> 00:09:16.460
I just can't keep still!

00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:25.290
Ran...

00:09:25.840 --> 00:09:28.330
I failed. Sorry.

00:09:28.330 --> 00:09:30.800
I know I made you spend all that time helping me train.

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:32.550
That's not...

00:09:32.550 --> 00:09:35.330
But I'm actually not that depressed.

00:09:35.330 --> 00:09:37.550
I feel like it was a clean loss.

00:09:39.050 --> 00:09:41.760
Ema-san was truly amazing.

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:46.060
She even made the top designer Tachibana-san stand up and applaud for her.

00:09:49.110 --> 00:09:51.320
That almost never happens.

00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:53.210
So she was <i>that</i> great...

00:09:53.210 --> 00:09:53.860
Yes.

00:09:53.860 --> 00:09:55.780
I wonder what that was like.

00:09:55.780 --> 00:10:00.470
The Headmistress told me that I gave a perfect performance.

00:10:00.470 --> 00:10:01.780
But still...

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:05.540
You can't become the designer's muse just by being perfect.

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:09.260
"Why didn't she choose you to be her muse?"

00:10:09.260 --> 00:10:11.040
Think carefully about the reason.

00:10:11.890 --> 00:10:15.110
I wonder what I can do to become her muse.

00:10:15.110 --> 00:10:16.450
"Muse"?

00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:28.280
What's a muse?

00:10:28.280 --> 00:10:29.600
Let's see...

00:10:30.460 --> 00:10:34.450
"Muses: Legendary goddess often 
appearing in ancient myths.

00:10:34.450 --> 00:10:39.150
Otherwise, those chosen as representative models within the fashion world."

00:10:39.150 --> 00:10:40.740
Wow, I didn't know that.

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:44.950
Come to think of it, there was 
something else the Headmistress said.

00:10:45.420 --> 00:10:48.710
The top designer Tachibana Anna gave me a message.

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:53.190
"What I'm searching for is not perfection, but a muse.

00:10:53.190 --> 00:10:55.630
You mustn't chase after me."

00:10:56.210 --> 00:10:57.590
You can't chase after her?

00:10:57.590 --> 00:10:58.440
Right.

00:10:58.440 --> 00:11:00.290
So you should stop running after her?

00:11:00.290 --> 00:11:02.100
I think that's a bit off.

00:11:02.100 --> 00:11:03.970
Then you should make her chase after you?

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:05.680
I'm <i>telling</i> you, that's the wrong track.

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:08.720
But it might not be far off.

00:11:09.460 --> 00:11:12.630
Either case, it means I'm not yet good enough.

00:11:12.630 --> 00:11:17.280
I need to try so hard that she becomes the one chasing after me.

00:11:18.020 --> 00:11:20.510
But Ran, you're always giving one hundred percent.

00:11:20.510 --> 00:11:23.000
I'll do the three hundred crunches with you.

00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:24.620
Listen, I'm telling you that's not it...

00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:26.990
No, now that it's come to this I'll do it.

00:11:27.980 --> 00:11:30.610
No matter how many hundreds of crunches it may take.

00:11:30.610 --> 00:11:32.120
Great!

00:11:33.010 --> 00:11:35.130
Ai... katsu! {I guess it works...}

00:11:35.130 --> 00:11:39.180
Ran, too fast! You're not supposed to be sprinting!

00:11:39.180 --> 00:11:41.400
Effort! It's all about the effort.

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:42.620
I guess so.

00:11:42.620 --> 00:11:44.590
You're slow! I'm gonna leave you behind.

00:11:44.590 --> 00:11:46.600
We're already being left behind...

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:50.140
But at least Ran's not feeling down after all that.

00:11:50.140 --> 00:11:52.020
I'd say she's a bit <i>too</i> energetic.

00:11:56.440 --> 00:12:00.680
Senpai, take a look at how reliable your underclassmen are.

00:12:00.680 --> 00:12:02.210
That's quite the pace.

00:12:02.210 --> 00:12:04.220
She's much faster than most idols.

00:12:04.220 --> 00:12:06.870
I bet she could even make the track team. {They have a track team;}

00:12:06.870 --> 00:12:09.170
We can't let our guards down.

00:12:09.170 --> 00:12:10.910
Back at you, Mizuki.

00:12:17.680 --> 00:12:19.400
Ran, you're too fast.

00:12:19.400 --> 00:12:21.120
I'm hitting my wall.

00:12:21.120 --> 00:12:23.630
Then I'm going ahead and doing another lap.

00:12:23.630 --> 00:12:28.940
Ran! We've got practice for the send-off
 party's fashion show later today.

00:12:30.790 --> 00:12:34.750
Sorry... I don't think I can be on a runway just yet.

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:36.630
Ran...

00:12:36.630 --> 00:12:39.390
I didn't realize she was actually feeling that sad.

00:12:39.390 --> 00:12:40.190
Same here.

00:12:46.420 --> 00:12:50.050
And so, as the day of the send-off party for the graduates slowly grew closer,

00:12:50.050 --> 00:12:55.960
we proceeded with the preparations without knowing whether or not Ran would appear in the fashion show.

00:12:57.420 --> 00:12:59.840
I wonder how Ran-tan is doing.

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:04.910
A fashion show without Ran-san is 
like a vampire without her fangs. {or like a waterbender without water}

00:13:06.030 --> 00:13:09.850
Anyway, I'm just saying that Yurika-sama is worried about her!

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:13.660
Me too. But I'm sure that Ran will...

00:13:13.660 --> 00:13:16.510
I understand your feelings of wanting her to come,

00:13:16.510 --> 00:13:19.860
but we still need to think about the worst case scenario.

00:13:19.860 --> 00:13:24.490
We need to focus on the graduating seniors who want to enjoy the fashion show.

00:13:24.490 --> 00:13:25.910
Yeah...

00:13:25.910 --> 00:13:26.950
But still—!

00:13:27.950 --> 00:13:30.490
But still, let's believe that Ran will come to us.

00:13:30.840 --> 00:13:31.990
Yeah!

00:13:34.620 --> 00:13:37.700
<i>How can I become her muse?</i>

00:13:37.700 --> 00:13:40.920
<i>How can I get her to chase after me...</i>

00:13:47.720 --> 00:13:48.840
Shibuki.

00:13:48.840 --> 00:13:50.280
Headmistress.

00:13:50.280 --> 00:13:53.140
When I look at you, I can't see a speck
 of enjoyment in your expression.

00:13:54.140 --> 00:13:55.570
Come with me.

00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:01.650
Why are we on the third-year's floor?

00:14:01.990 --> 00:14:03.650
Look at these.

00:14:03.650 --> 00:14:05.250
Wow...

00:14:05.250 --> 00:14:06.650
They're so stylish.

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:08.780
It's not just their style.

00:14:09.180 --> 00:14:11.530
Everyone's having fun.

00:14:11.530 --> 00:14:13.430
Don't you think so?

00:14:13.430 --> 00:14:14.540
I do.

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:18.000
All of them are photos that 
Shinjou Ema did the styling for.

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:19.290
Ema-san did them?

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:22.290
That girl truly loves western-style clothes.

00:14:22.460 --> 00:14:25.300
She can have fun both wearing them and dressing others up.

00:14:26.190 --> 00:14:30.760
I wonder if being around her makes the other girls naturally want to be more stylish?

00:14:31.310 --> 00:14:36.060
This class has a particularly large 
percentage of fashionable students.

00:14:36.060 --> 00:14:39.490
She can influence her classmates that much... {so to that}

00:14:39.490 --> 00:14:41.810
Ema-san really is amazing.

00:14:41.810 --> 00:14:44.050
It's not just her classmates.

00:14:44.050 --> 00:14:46.840
That girl has also influenced several designers.

00:14:46.840 --> 00:14:48.560
Even designers?

00:14:48.560 --> 00:14:52.210
Shibuki. If you want to continue working as a model,

00:14:52.210 --> 00:14:54.880
then you must understand the true meaning of being a muse.

00:14:55.600 --> 00:14:59.850
Muses... they are the legendary 
goddesses who appear in myths.

00:15:01.010 --> 00:15:04.130
They are both beautiful and wise.

00:15:04.130 --> 00:15:10.340
It's said that each individual's unique traits have given inspiration to a large number of artists.

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:16.100
It is <i>because</i> muses existed that artists were able to create their masterpieces.

00:15:16.450 --> 00:15:19.450
Artists and designers are, after all, only human.

00:15:19.450 --> 00:15:23.920
If something stimulates or influences them, then they'll give birth to a new work of art.

00:15:25.430 --> 00:15:27.110
Aren't you the same?

00:15:27.110 --> 00:15:32.200
Your close friends saw how much effort you were putting in and decided to do the same.

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:33.110
Right.

00:15:33.110 --> 00:15:35.240
Designers are the same.

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:40.370
That's why in the world of fashion, those who can awaken the creative spark in designers

00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:42.330
are called "muses".

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:44.130
Then Ema-san is...

00:15:44.900 --> 00:15:47.810
She made Spicy Ageha's designer, Tachibana Anna,

00:15:47.810 --> 00:15:52.260
strongly feel that she wanted to design for her.

00:15:54.120 --> 00:15:56.970
That explains her applause...

00:15:57.800 --> 00:16:01.940
That's why she left the message 
"You mustn't chase after me."

00:16:02.820 --> 00:16:05.030
Become a superb muse.

00:16:05.030 --> 00:16:08.980
A muse that would make any 
designer want to chase after you.

00:16:09.910 --> 00:16:11.360
I will.

00:16:12.380 --> 00:16:14.110
This is from Tachibana Anna.

00:16:14.110 --> 00:16:16.870
She said to give them to you once you smiled again. {I'm losing it here} {You lose things too easily}

00:16:19.660 --> 00:16:20.840
These are...

00:16:27.140 --> 00:16:29.380
And on the day of the graduation ceremony...

00:16:30.280 --> 00:16:34.890
To all of our third-years, we 
congratulate you on your graduation.

00:16:34.890 --> 00:16:39.800
We will shortly begin the send-off party organized by the underclassmen.

00:16:39.800 --> 00:16:41.390
Please relax and enjoy.

00:16:44.770 --> 00:16:46.020
It's finally time.

00:16:46.020 --> 00:16:47.870
Yep, the preparations are perfect!

00:16:47.870 --> 00:16:49.740
All the seats are packed!

00:16:49.740 --> 00:16:52.780
The concert hall is overflowing 
with soon-to-be graduates!

00:16:52.780 --> 00:16:57.450
I suppose it was worth it for Yurika-sama to tell them that I'd suck their blood if they didn't show up.

00:16:57.450 --> 00:16:59.980
So you talked to everyone, Yurika-chan.

00:16:59.980 --> 00:17:01.410
Sort of...

00:17:01.410 --> 00:17:02.690
All that's left is...

00:17:02.690 --> 00:17:04.160
To wait for the lead girl!

00:17:04.160 --> 00:17:05.210
Yeah.

00:17:10.900 --> 00:17:11.970
Sorry I'm late.

00:17:11.970 --> 00:17:12.650
Ran!

00:17:12.650 --> 00:17:14.040
We never doubted...

00:17:14.040 --> 00:17:14.970
That you'd come! {kawa-fucking-ii, Yurika}

00:17:15.970 --> 00:17:17.720
Er, I mean...

00:17:17.720 --> 00:17:23.480
H-How dare you keep me waiting? It's two hundred and fifty years too early for you to even consider that!

00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:25.980
Sorry for making you worry.

00:17:25.980 --> 00:17:30.190
But we all believed that you would eventually come.

00:17:31.880 --> 00:17:33.180
Thank you.

00:17:33.180 --> 00:17:36.140
It's almost time. Ran, standby ready. {Set up}

00:17:36.140 --> 00:17:37.550
Same to you all.

00:17:38.240 --> 00:17:40.710
Let's all go up together.

00:17:40.710 --> 00:17:42.660
I already have your outfits picked.

00:17:42.660 --> 00:17:43.720
Those are...

00:17:43.720 --> 00:17:45.620
Spicy Ageha cards?

00:17:46.520 --> 00:17:48.130
This is for Ichigo.

00:17:48.130 --> 00:17:49.910
This one is Aoi's.

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:52.380
These for Otome.

00:17:52.380 --> 00:17:54.380
And this for Yurika.

00:17:55.390 --> 00:17:56.270
They're wonderful!

00:17:56.270 --> 00:17:56.840
Yes.

00:17:56.840 --> 00:17:57.900
Love you!

00:17:57.900 --> 00:18:01.390
Lets show our seniors just how good we can look.

00:18:01.390 --> 00:18:06.140
I want to show them how amazing the 
underclassmen they're leaving behind are.

00:18:06.140 --> 00:18:08.020
Everyone's on board, right?

00:18:08.550 --> 00:18:10.020
Yeah!

00:18:12.070 --> 00:18:15.570
<i>One day I'll become a true muse!</i>

00:19:27.700 --> 00:19:32.520
<i>I won't lose to these cards... I'll fly!</i>

00:20:21.570 --> 00:20:24.070
Nice job, I can feel your joy.

00:21:24.380 --> 00:21:25.890
Great job, everyone.

00:21:25.890 --> 00:21:28.720
You too! That was amazing, Ran!

00:21:28.720 --> 00:21:30.140
Yeah, you were the best!

00:21:30.140 --> 00:21:33.380
Same to you. I've never felt that good before.

00:21:33.380 --> 00:21:36.140
Otome's touched! I'm about to cry!

00:21:36.140 --> 00:21:37.930
Well, as for me...

00:21:37.930 --> 00:21:38.560
Sorry!

00:21:38.560 --> 00:21:39.960
I need to go!

00:21:52.340 --> 00:21:53.660
Shinjou-senpai!

00:21:54.610 --> 00:21:55.910
Shibuki-san.

00:21:58.050 --> 00:22:01.600
I promise I'll make it up to the same stage as you one day.

00:22:02.220 --> 00:22:03.430
Then come on up.

00:22:03.430 --> 00:22:05.420
And one day I'll surpass you.

00:22:06.660 --> 00:22:08.180
I'll be waiting for you.

00:22:10.680 --> 00:22:12.870
This is a wonderful academy.

00:22:12.870 --> 00:22:14.430
Good job, me!

00:22:14.430 --> 00:22:17.440
Just to remind you, you barely did anything.

00:22:17.440 --> 00:22:18.440
What?!

00:23:55.660 --> 00:23:57.870
This week's Aikatsu Aphorism!

00:23:58.750 --> 00:24:00.750
How was the coord I chose?

00:24:00.750 --> 00:24:02.680
It was wonderful!

00:24:02.680 --> 00:24:05.070
It's pretty fun to think about other girls' coords too.

00:24:05.070 --> 00:24:07.460
I'll pick one out for you next time.

00:24:07.850 --> 00:24:10.010
Fashion begins with a smile.

00:24:10.620 --> 00:24:11.880
We've got some time off, girls.

00:24:11.880 --> 00:24:13.720
That has an idol-y ring to it!

00:24:13.720 --> 00:24:15.220
I'm so happy we've got a vacation!

00:24:15.220 --> 00:24:17.140
It's our first off together.

00:24:17.140 --> 00:24:18.390
Let's have fun!

00:24:18.760 --> 00:24:19.980
Next time on Aikatsu!

00:24:19.980 --> 00:24:21.410
Enjoy Off Time.

00:24:21.410 --> 00:24:24.040
Always passionate, Idol Activities!
